-------------
VERSION 1.0.0
-------------
* Remove redundant proportion and cumulative proportion columns from all
  univariate frequency tables: categorical, ordinal and numerical. Retain
  percentages based on non-missing observations and update explanatory notes.
* Add empirical and normalized Gini coefficients under one Numerical Data
  option, and an independent Lorenz curve using the jamovi theme and palette.
  Explain unsupported data and undefined normalization for a single value.
* Explain unavailable ordinal association indices without changing defined
  zeros; clear notes after recovery and preserve directional Somers behavior.
* Keep grouped Q-Q/ECDF messages legible without hiding valid groups.
* Hide nominal frequency, association and prediction tables independently
  when none of their output options is selected; remove blank placeholders.
* Preserve variable category order in pie, doughnut and lollipop plots;
  retain decreasing frequency order in Pareto plots.
* Omit undefined fitted normal curves for constant or single-observation
  samples, with an explanation, while retaining other groups' curves.
* Use consecutive footnote letters in normality tables and remove obsolete
  explanations when data or selected tests change.
* Retain the Mann-Whitney Hodges-Lehmann estimate with one observation per
  group, but report confidence limits as unavailable with an explanation.
* Explain unavailable Mann-Whitney Hodges-Lehmann confidence intervals when
  all observations are tied, instead of exposing an internal R error.
* Use explicit a/b/c footnote markers in Mann-Whitney tables; jmvcore
  superscript letters omit c. Preserve Hodges-Lehmann failure explanations
  after writing the result row.
* Keep median plot groups in their original order when only some groups have
  finite confidence limits.
* Place Mann-Whitney median plot legends below the panel and wrap long text
  so the legend cannot squeeze the two groups out of view.
* Combine median interval explanations into one footnote per group so
  confidence and unbounded-interval messages share a single marker.
* Compute Mann-Whitney exact group median intervals from the binomial sign
  distribution, including infinite endpoints when the requested confidence
  cannot be attained with a finite interval in small samples.
* Mann-Whitney group median intervals preserve each group's result and native
  confidence metadata independently, report unbounded limits explicitly,
  and use plot legends that distinguish finite from unbounded intervals.
* Mann-Whitney probability of superiority now counts between-group ties as
  one half, consistently with the reported U statistic and direction note.
* Preserve the paired Hodges-Lehmann estimate for a single complete pair,
  but report its confidence interval as unavailable rather than confidence 0%.
  Median plot legends identify when no confidence limits are available.
* Draw the continuous-density query marker as one annotated segment, avoiding
  repeated scalar aesthetics and ggplot2 warnings.
* Uniform distribution queries now accept values and interval bounds outside
  the support, returning the corresponding zero densities and tail probabilities.
* Unified discrete and continuous probability highlights using the second
  jamovi palette fill (yellow in the default palette); unselected discrete
  bars use the first fill (blue). Explicit mappings follow the global theme.
* Restored visible shading in continuous cumulative, survival, interval and
  quantile plots by using the jamovi accent fill rather than its background fill.
* Numerical Q-Q plots now explain constant or insufficient finite data in the
  plot area instead of silently disappearing.
* Removed duplicate footnote markers from unavailable mixed-data effect sizes
  and formatted the H in Kruskal-Wallis eta-squared as a subscript.
* Fixed ordinal heatmap and alluvial frequency gradients being replaced by
  the global jamovi discrete palette; declared plot-selection dependencies
  so ordinal image resources refresh when plot combinations change.
* Removed notches from numerical bivariate marginal box plots.
* Added frequency tables to univariate Numerical Data, with distinct observed
  values in ascending numeric order, cumulative counts and relative values,
  valid-observation denominators and no odds or automatic interval grouping.
* Reorganised categorical statistics into two aligned columns and moved the
  category-count field below IQV, with an explicit automatic-zero label.
* Restricted univariate Categorical Data to nominal selections. Its frequency
  and odds tables no longer contain cumulative columns.
* Added optional frequency tables to Ordinal Data, including counts,
  proportions, percentages and cumulative values in defined category order,
  without odds. Missing observations are reported separately and excluded
  from relative-frequency denominators and cumulative values.
* Corrected symmetric Goodman-Kruskal lambda using pooled prediction errors;
  removed the unsupported symmetric Goodman-Kruskal tau.
* Replaced H1/H3 with percentile skewness coefficients SP50/SP80.
* Ordinal analyses distinguish ordered text categories from numeric scores.
  Text summaries preserve category order; numeric summaries retain stored
  values, including zero and unequal spacing.
* Numeric-only ordinal controls are disabled for text-only selections.
  Range is omitted for text-only selections, and mixed selections include
  cell footnotes for statistics that require numeric values.
* Bivariate numerical analyses explain undefined correlations and their
  squared values with cell footnotes when either variable is constant.
  Covariance remains available, and footnotes are removed when variability
  is restored.
* Corrected marginal histogram and box-plot orientation in numerical
  bivariate scatterplots so each marginal follows its corresponding axis.
* Restored example dataset registration in the jamovi Data Library
  and added Anscombe's quartet.
* Empty defined categories are retained in frequency tables when requested
  and excluded from association calculations, with explanatory notes.
* Corrected geometric mean and geometric standard deviation, Yule's V,
  Wilson's e and Chuprov's T.
* Corrected paired Hodges-Lehmann estimates and confidence intervals,
  Wilcoxon rank-biserial correlation, Mann-Whitney average ranks and
  tie-corrected z statistics, and one-sided normal-approximation p-values.
* Improved confidence-interval handling, selected-pair extraction and
  Wilcoxon rank descriptives, with three rows per pair.
* Normality tests run only when selected, handle failures individually,
  and correctly populate grouped results. Added an inference caveat for
  Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests with estimated normal parameters.
* Corrected grouped ECDF and Q-Q plots and within-group standardisation.
  Q-Q plotting no longer requires qqplotr or qqconf.
* Improved discrete and continuous distribution validation, plotting ranges,
  probability labels and handling of endpoint and degenerate cases.
* Corrected bivariate plots for variable names containing spaces.
* Improved handling of missing, empty, constant and invalid inputs,
  per-statistic error reporting, result invalidation and dependent controls.
* Added compatibility with jmvcore versions without a translation marker
  or an analysis translation method.
* Added Solanas et al. (2005) to all seven descriptive analyses.
  Standardised reference author formatting and adopted the recommended
  methodological citations for effectsize and WRS2.
* Updated dependency declarations and improved plot rendering and restoration.


-------------
VERSION 0.1.2
-------------
*Description and 000.yaml modified.
*Univariate Ordinal and Numerical; and Bivariate Mixed Data: label for quartiles' average is now midhinge.
*Bivariate Mixed Data: Data stacked aes() dependence error now solved.
*Continuous variables: stat_function() dependence error now solved.
*Error in z's Wilcoxon's test computation now solved.


-------------
VERSION 0.1.1
-------------
*First public version available at jamovi library

* Paired Wilcoxon Hodges-Lehmann intervals now retain R's returned confidence
  level and explain differences from the requested level in a cell footnote.
* HL confidence headings now display the level returned by R. Unreachable
  requested levels use a concise note; different levels across pairs are
  identified per row under a neutral confidence-interval heading.
* Remove field-width padding from HL confidence percentages in headings and
  notes without changing interval calculations.
* Explicitly trim formatted HL confidence percentages to remove remaining padding.
* Explain unavailable paired HL intervals when every paired difference is zero,
  avoiding a misleading zero-confidence heading.
